Changes:
 lightdm (1.32.0-6ubuntu4+unity2) resolute; urgency=medium
 .
   * d/p/0010-session-child-finish-the-cleanup-when-SIGTERM-arrive.patch:
     when SIGTERM reaches session-child after the session process has
     ended, finish the cleanup (X authority removal, PAM session close)
     instead of quitting, with a 10 s alarm in case it blocks. A greeter is
     stopped by both logind and the daemon; the second SIGTERM cut the
     greeter's cleanup short in most greeter stops and could leave its X
     cookie, valid for the user's display, in lightdm's .Xauthority.
